    "findings": [
      "All 19 new individual datasets match independently selected raw field or accepted-step history arrays, including profile selections and time/depth/step coordinates. All 61 event footprints and classifications were checked against threshold-crossing slip.",
      "Panel labels, units, legends, color scales and depth axes are legible in all six composites. The F3b depth label is also present in the individual PDF text.",
      "The final complete cycle spans years 168.1853495116306 to 199.62331125467733, or 31.43796174304674 years, versus approximately 32 years in the published Fig. 2c. All six recurrence intervals are retained; their median is 27.071324686266404 years. This does not establish a stationary cycle.",
      "F2c shows upward fronts, partial ruptures and a late swarm, but also an early shallow rupture at 0.13217 years after opening. The first two chronological partial footprints are 0.01335--5.74303 km and 12.13264--17.14516 km. No event is discarded to imitate the published phase sequence.",
      "F2d retains two complete cycles. Final shallowest cumulative slip is 2.772747039794922 m and maximum cumulative slip is 3.6112899780273438 m. The slip scale is similar to the published figure, but individual contours differ.",
      "F3 gives a 28.110528 MPa stress range at the saved depth 10.004043579 km, exceeding the article's stated order 10--20 MPa variation. Permeability ranges from 4.320249051066589e-19 to 3.5755253878008025e-16 m^2 and maximum upward flux there is 3.6743102782565984e-08 m/s. The stress maximum at 19.4411 years is a diagnostic, not the authors' phase boundary.",
